  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing conflict sensitivity: training for Korean stakeholders in conflict and fragile environmentsEnhancing conflict sensitivity: training for Korean stakeholders in conflict and fragile environments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the capacity of key stakeholders involved in KOICA&apos;s Conflict and Fragility Programme through a comprehensive conflict analysis training. The primary participants of this training will be approximately 30 individuals drawn from KOICA staff, officials from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MOFA), and Korean NGO representatives who are either currently engaged in or interested in the Conflict and Fragility Programme. The immersive training will be delivered to the selected 30 participants, providing an interactive environment to consolidate learning. At KOICA&apos;s specific request, the training will emphasize how best to integrate conflict analysis into KOICA&apos;s Conflict and Fragility Programme. Participants will engage with realistic scenario-based case studies designed to foster practical application and deepen their analytical skills. This hands-on approach will equip them with actionable tools to incorporate conflict sensitivity into project design, implementation, and monitoring. Through this initiative, IOM aims to enhance the capacity of KOICA, MOFA, and Korean NGO staff to design and implement development interventions that are both conflict-sensitive and aligned with international best practices.</narrative>
  </description>
